{title: For I’m sheltered in the arms of God}
{x_theme: heaven}
{x_source: docx:1. Incomplete/For I’m sheltered in the arms of God..docx}

{comment: Chorus}
So let the storm rage high, the dark clouds rise.
They don’t worry me
For I’m sheltered, safe, within the arms of God.
He walks with me, and no divert shall harm me.
For I’m sheltered in the arms of God.

{comment: Verse 1}
I feel the touch of hands so kind and tender.
They’re leading me in paths that I must try.
I’ll have no fear, For Jesus walks beside me.
For I’m sheltered in the arms of God.

{comment: Verse 2}
Soon I shall feel the cold from Heaven’s portals.
Come home my child, It’s the last mile you must trot.
I’ll fall asleep and wake up in God’s new-held arms,
For I’m sheltered in the arms of God.
